      "body": "## Motivation\n\nCI runs each registered test file as `python file.py`. `test/registered/unit/distributed/test_parallel_state.py` defines 8 tests, but its hand-written `__main__` calls only the 4 the file was written with (6 cases). Four pytest-style tests added later have never run in CI:\n\n- `test_deterministic_reduce_scatter_preserves_input_and_selects_rank_shard` (#38160)\n- `test_deterministic_reduce_scatterv_selects_rank_shard` (#38160)\n- `test_nondeterministic_reduce_scatter_keeps_native_path` (#38160)\n- `test_custom_allreduce_precedes_symmetric_memory_pynccl` (#35061)\n\nThey also rely on `@pytest.mark.parametrize` and the `monkeypatch` fixture, which the hand-written runner can't supply.\n\n## Modifications\n\n- Replace the hand-written `__main__` with `sys.exit(pytest.main([__file__]))`, the same entry point 89 other registered files use, so pytest collects every test, parametrization and fixture.\n\n## Accuracy Tests\n\nNot applicable; test-only change.\n\n## Speed Tests and Profiling\n\nNot applicable. This draft relies on its own CI run as the test. The `base-a-test-cpu` log for this file should report `32 passed`, up from 6 hand-called cases today. `est_time` may need a bump if the file runs noticeably longer.\n\n## Checklist\n\n- [ ] Format your code according to the [Format code with pre-commit](https://docs.sglang.io/developer_guide/contribution_guide.html#format-code-with-pre-commit).\n- [x] Add unit tests according to the [Run and add unit tests](https://docs.sglang.io/developer_guide/contribution_guide.html#run-and-add-unit-tests).\n- [ ] Update documentation according to [Write documentations](https://docs.sglang.io/developer_guide/contribution_guide.html#write-documentations).\n- [ ] Provide accuracy and speed benchmark results according to [Test the accuracy](https://docs.sglang.io/developer_guide/contribution_guide.html#test-the-accuracy) and [Benchmark the speed](https://docs.sglang.io/developer_guide/contribution_guide.html#benchmark-the-speed).\n- [x] Follow the SGLang code style [guidance](https://docs.sglang.io/developer_guide/contribution_guide.html#code-style-guidance).\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\n<!-- pr-states:start -->\n---\n### CI States\n\nLatest PR Test (Base): <!-- slot:pr-test:start -->:x: [Run #39520732852](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/39520732852)<!-- slot:pr-test:end -->\nLatest PR Test (Extra): <!-- slot:pr-test-extra:start -->:x: [Run #39520732925](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/39520732925)<!-- slot:pr-test-extra:end -->\nLatest PR Test (AMD ROCm 10): <!-- slot:pr-test-amd:start -->:x: [Run #39520732818](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/39520732818)<!-- slot:pr-test-amd:end -->\n<!-- pr-states:end -->",
